// §14 entry 22 -- `u4:maior` (explicit byte order on a SUB-byte field) ->
// EXS-E0201 ("unexpected token").
//
// §5.2 "Bit-width fields", rule 3: "Byte order is required above 8 bits
// and is not part of the grammar AT OR BELOW IT. An unannotated multi-byte
// field in a `@transitus` type IS `:nativus` and is therefore already
// EXS-E0321; `u4:maior` does not parse, so it is EXS-E0201. Neither needs a
// new code." One code, not two.
//
// RUNS since b86b080 (2026-09-25). History, kept short: this fixture once
// read status=run on a PRESENCE check of EXS-E0201; tightening
// tests/run.sh to the exact code set found exsc also emitted EXS-E0322 --
// the wire-layout pass evaluated `campus: u4` over what the parser's
// recovery left behind (the parser keeps the `:maior` suffix for the
// round trip and raises E0201; there is no Error node to skip). §5.2 rule
// 3 says one code fires, not two. b86b080 treats a sub-byte integer field
// carrying a byte order -- a shape rule 3 says cannot be written -- as
// recovery debris and silences the layout pass for that struct; entry 21's
// legal-shape E0322 still fires (tests/unit/chk_row_layout_debris.asm).
// Measured on the main tree at fe24fe5: exactly {EXS-E0201}, exit 1.

@transitus
publica structura Malum2 {
    campus: u4:maior
}

// TEST: entry=22 shape=code expect-code=EXS-E0201 status=run
